[strong: HER.] A dead man too.

[strong: DIO.] And no one shall persuade me not to go after the man.

[strong: HER.] Do you mean below, to Hades?

[strong: DIO.] And lower still, if there's a lower still.

[strong: HER.] What on earth for?

@style verse
  [strong: DIO.] I want a genuine poet, "For some are not, and those that are, are bad."

[strong: HER.] What! does not Iophon live?

@style verse
  [strong: DIO.] Well, he's the sole Good thing remaining, if even he is good.
  For even of that I'm not exactly certain.

@style verse
  [strong: HER.] If go you must, there's Sophocles—he comes Before Euripides—why not take [italic: him]?

@style verse
  [strong: DIO.] Not till I've tried if Iophon's coin rings true
